Targets: wasm
Subject: Provide POSIX and System V semaphores for a single-process WebAssembly build
Purpose: Emscripten without threads links sem_init(), sem_trywait() and the other semaphore calls, but they are stubs: sem_init() fails and sem_trywait() always succeeds, so PGSemaphoreReset() (called by InitProcess) calls sem_trywait() until it fails and never returns; postgres --boot and --single spin at full CPU right after set_max_safe_fds. With a single process a semaphore is only a counter, so the five calls PostgreSQL uses (sem_init, sem_destroy, sem_post, sem_trywait, sem_wait) are defined in wasm_sema.c under other names and posix_sema.c is given them by macros (the C library's own definitions cannot be replaced: they sit in an object the link needs for other symbols). A wait on a zero semaphore, which nothing could ever post, fails with EDEADLK (PostgreSQL reports it as a FATAL error) instead of hanging. Compiled only when __EMSCRIPTEN__ is defined.
Components: src/backend/port/wasm_sema.c (new), src/include/port/wasm_sema.h (new), src/backend/port/posix_sema.c, src/backend/port/Makefile
Checks: postgres --boot and --single start under node and get past InitProcess (scripts/build-wasm.sh creates the template data directory, scripts/test-wasm-node.sh)
Origin: own
Adaptation-note: releases before 10 select System V semaphores on Linux (unnamed POSIX ones need thread safety there); wasm_sema.c therefore also emulates semget, semctl and semop with counters in process memory (a wait that could never end fails with EDEADLK).
Ported-from: 9.6.24 (wasm/pg9-6/0005-wasm-semaphores.patch) for 9.5.25 by scripts/port-patches.js
